openvino_bevfusion: make room for ten lidar sweeps.

BEVFusion is trained on the nuScenes key frame plus its 9 previous lidar
sweeps, with the time lag of each sweep as the 5th point column, but the
export only accepts 70000 points and 60000 voxels: one sweep. Ten sweeps are
up to 10 x 34752 points (32 beams x 1086 firings); on nuScenes mini they give
83000 voxels on average and up to 136000.

Accept 350000 points and 160000 voxels, BEVFusion's test-time max_voxels,
and double the voxelize hash table to 2^18 slots so it stays at most ~60%
full. run_inference_standalone.py and config.py load 9 sweeps, as the
reference test pipeline does. The model weights are unchanged; a single
sweep still runs exactly as before.

Remove this patch once openvino_contrib carries an equivalent change.

